==== stdout ====
Usage: raphael update <path> [changes] [options]
       raphael update --id <id> [changes] [options]

Change an item with revision protection.

Give at least one change. Tags replace the complete tag list; --no-tags clears it. A renamed title does not change the path.

A body replacement requires the revision you read. Other changes may read and pin the current id and revision for you. Conflicts are never retried automatically.

Rules:
  Metadata is set once, at create. --active and --inactive apply only to projects.
  On a revision conflict, get the item again and reconcile your intended change before updating with its new revision.

Options:
      --id <id>
      Address by durable id instead of path.
      --title <text>
      Name, at most 200 characters.
      --description <text>
      Description, at most 4000 characters. An empty string clears it.
      --slug <slug>
      Address within the parent, at most 100 characters. See help addressing.
      --body <text|@file|@->
      Body text, @file, or @- for stdin. An empty string clears it; updates require --revision.
      --body-literal <text>
      Literal body text, including text beginning with @. Updates require --revision.
      --body-format <format>
      Submitted body: markdown or tiptap. Default: markdown.
      --tag <tag>
      Repeat for each tag; at most 25 tags of 50 characters. Commas are refused. Updates replace all tags. Repeatable.
      --no-tags
      Clear all tags.
      --active
      Mark the project active.
      --inactive
      Mark the project inactive.
      --revision <n>
      Revision read previously. Without a body change, omitted revisions are read immediately before sending.
      --return-format <format>
      Returned body: markdown or tiptap. Requires --json. Default: markdown.
      --json
      Print one JSON result.
  -h, --help
      Show this help.

Examples:
  raphael update /work/raphael/api-design --body '# Revised design' --revision 8
  raphael update /work/raphael --tag reviewed --tag contracts
  raphael update --id 42 --title 'Contract review' --description ''

Prints:
  The updated item and revision. JSON carries `entity`.

Next: raphael get --id 42

See also: raphael help revisions; raphael help content
